{"id": 4, "ts": 1780561208.7375736, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical strengths outweigh his unfriendly demeanor, which could undermine crew cooperation and professional communication in the cockpit. While A can anticipate dangerous situations and has excellent spatial vision, his noted unfriendly attitude raises a serious concern for the collaborative environment required on long\u2011distance flights.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates strong reliability and stress resilience\u2014he is very conscientious and handles stress very well, both critical for consistent, safe operations. His ability to assess weather conditions and his excellent computer skills further support his technical competence. Although he is regarded as pretentious and sometimes adopts the wrong tone, these communication issues appear less severe than outright hostility or egocentric behavior and can be addressed through targeted training.\nGiven the balance of reliability, stress handling, and technical capability, I would provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fB for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
